Concept_Name: blade servers
Core_Definition: A hardware technology consisting of a single chassis that houses multiple individual computers, each referred to as a blade.
Key_Actors: Individual computers on blades; physical machine chassis; teams responsible for hardware installation.
Operational_Workflow: They are used to simplify the preparation of physical machines; they make the installation and maintenance processes easier by allowing multiple computers to be handled within a single chassis.
