Concept_Name: Installation and Testing
Core_Definition: The phase of the project schedule where software packages are deployed on hardware and verified before deployment to the production cluster.
Key_Actors: Project authors or assigned FTEs; systems being monitored.
Operational_Workflow: This stage occurs after hardware procurement and lasts two days; it involves installing Debian Linux using the standard corporate server configuration, installing the server software package, and installing client packages on all systems being monitored.
Rules_and_Constraints: Installation must use the standard corporate server configuration; specific software packages like bosun-server and bosun-client must be used.
