Concept_Name: Security Operations
Core_Definition: A functional role or team responsible for reviewing and approving security and privacy ramifications within a design document.
Key_Actors: Security Operations team; Project authors; Technical leads; Director of Operations.
Operational_Workflow: The team reviews the security concerns section of a design document to ensure mitigations are sufficient; they specifically evaluate methods for storing sensitive data such as SNMP community strings in password vaults; once satisfied, they provide a formal approval date that is recorded in the document status.
